WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.470
- Hi everyone, my name is Vig.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.610
- And I'm Juan.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.000
We are your senior class officers.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.350
Welcome to the Class Day 2020 experience.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.300
- First and foremost,

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.070
we really hope everyone
is safe and healthy.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.970
This is obviously not what we envisioned

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.290
when we pictured the
end of our time at Yale.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.200
These last few weeks were
supposed to be some of the best

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.020
and instead they've been
some of the toughest.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.800
But those lost weeks

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.280
will not be what defines
the Class of 2020.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.210
No, we're the class that
pressed on in spite of the virus

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.420
and all the barriers that it brought.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.030
We made TikToks, had Zoom happy hours,

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:45.900
we passionately advocated for UP.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.900
More than that, we had an incredible

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.420
3.75 years together on campus

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.800
and stayed together virtually
in that last quarter.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.380
We are still connected
despite the physical distance

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.240
that this pandemic has forced on us.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.580
We will not be the class that
simply lost our senior spring,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.560
but instead the one that persevered

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.020
through all the adversity that we faced.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.350
- Our time at Yale has been
marked by momentous change.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.960
We are among the last first
years to experience Commons

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.080
in all its traditions and glory,

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.790
and we will hopefully be the last class

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.963
to hear jokes that TD is so far.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.300
We were the first to
have Heads of College,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.650
first years, and Hopper College.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.580
Yale Memes for Special Snowflake Teens

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.133
was founded when we got here.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:35.770
We were witness to the
unforgettable month of November 2016

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:38.180
when we won our first
Harvard-Yale game in 10 years

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.560
and then went on to win two more.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.230
- Then senior year happened

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:45.610
and we learned how much
this class loved to party.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.490
We kicked things off with Opening Night

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.560
and we had two open bars.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.800
But we realized we needed
to upgrade pretty soon.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.870
And so we did, to 12 at Masquerade.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.790
We had Oktoberfest

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:01.970
a month after Oktoberfest
is supposed to happen,

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.580
and we finished things off
with our Wine and Cheese Night

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.320
at the Yale Center for British Art

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.150
which is definitely the kind of event

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.790
that I expected to have more of at Yale.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:13.060
And before you ask, I'm sorry,

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.453
it is too late to get your senior sticker.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.920
- All of those big moments
would not have been complete

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.540
without the smaller ones.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.187
From Junzi late night, staying
way too long at the Buttery,

00:02:24.187 --> 00:02:26.300
"Living on a Prayer" to close out Woads,

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.770
to IMs, the bonds we formed

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.570
and the memories we made together

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.703
will be what define our time at Yale.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.630
From academics to clubs,
residential colleges and the arts,

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.763
cultural centers and athletic teams,

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.470
there are people and
friendships that have helped us

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.550
through Yale and will continue to help us

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.410
throughout our lives.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.703
This is how our class will be remembered.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.960
- So congratulations to the Class of 2020.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.580
We are so excited to see

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.880
what the future holds for all of us.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.280
Even though our in-person celebration

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.230
is gonna have to wait a little bit,

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.400
we can graduate knowing
that we have each other

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.080
to help us get there.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.740
And when we do, I think we're gonna need

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.980
to have more than 12 open bars.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.990
- In the meantime, we
will continue to celebrate

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:14.830
your hard work despite this change.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.930
We'll now move on to
the Class Day committee

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.940
who have worked tirelessly to modify

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:21.100
the traditional Class Day experience

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.823
to make it special for a class
that deserves nothing less.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.250
- Thanks Vig and Juan.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.510
To the Class of 2020, on behalf of myself,

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:32.570
Ananya, Calvin, Nathan, and Sarah,

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.720
we just wanna say congratulations.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.180
The past couple of years have been filled

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.730
with so many fantastic
memories and experiences

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.140
that only feel sweeter to us now.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.680
We've worked really
hard over the past year

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.420
to craft a celebration of
the amazing experiences,

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.840
accomplishments, friendships, and bonds

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.340
that we've built together as a class

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.720
and we are so excited to
showcase the amazing work

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.030
of our classmates to you this week.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.130
This year being virtual,

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.540
we've done our best to revamp
the Class Day experience

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.070
to make it more accessible
to you all and your families,

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:02.380
regardless of where you are in the world.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.670
- So instead of Class Day,
this year we're excited

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.070
to be expanding this tradition

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:10.670
into a week-long celebration
we're calling Class Week.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:13.180
Each day this week we
will be releasing a video

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.340
covering a portion of the
typical Class Day elements.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.500
These videos will be
posted at 2:30 p.m. Eastern

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:20.930
under the Class Day tab

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:25.930
of the Yale Commencement 2020
website, yale2020.yale.edu.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.730
Because this is happening
over the course of a week,

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.690
we hope you will stay engaged every day

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.683
and join us in celebrating
our amazing class.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.420
- Each portion of the
ceremony will have its own day

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.830
and we have a little preview

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.440
of all the exciting
content coming your way.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.790
On Tuesday, we begin the week

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:46.430
with Joy Qiu's "Serious Reflection,"

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.930
as she thinks about what
Yale has meant to her

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.120
and about what graduating
means to all of us.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.080
On Wednesday, Simon Fraser

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.520
and Oscar Lopez-Aguirre will present us

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.717
with their extremely funny
"Comedic Reflection."

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.030
On Thursday, Vincent Vaughns
will give us his "Ivy Ode,"

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.910
an inspiring call to all of
us to recognize our dreams

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.650
and fight for them.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.790
Come Friday, Dean Chun
will offer his remarks

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.583
to the Class of 2020.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.680
And after that we suggest
that you grab some Kleenex

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.210
in preparation for the
next item on the agenda

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.833
which is the class history slideshow.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.650
On Saturday, we have an
exciting toast prepared

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.793
with some very special guests.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:35.000
And finally, on Sunday, we end
with the week with an address

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.240
from our esteemed guest
speaker, Dr. Jean Bennett,

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.763
the Class of 1976.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.760
- As Sarah walked us through the schedule,

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.280
you can see that we've
adapted certain traditions

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.080
of the Class Day ceremony.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:50.040
The virtual format lends
itself to week-long festivities

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.220
that we can all enjoy together.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.750
In our virtual ceremony
we've found some traditions

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:58.010
work very well while others
are harder to replicate.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:00.110
During most years, students and speakers

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.470
sport homemade hats during the ceremony.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:04.410
This year however, we encourage you

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.330
to dedicate your time and supplies

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:09.960
to making masks for your friends,
families, and communities.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.753
We've learned time and time again at Yale

00:06:11.753 --> 00:06:14.090
that the small actions matter.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:16.140
Right now, we can make that difference

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.100
with this small action.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.480
Whether you decide to make masks or hats,

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.530
please share your progress
with the class on social media

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.640
using the hashtag #Yale2020.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:28.250
And we will be sure to include hats

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.800
in our future in-person ceremony.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.460
We are also shipping a
Class Day care package

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:36.400
with the physical items from
a typical Class Day ceremony

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.840
and some new additions.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.133
Look forward to that.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.617
- We have an exciting week planned ahead

00:06:42.617 --> 00:06:45.460
and we cannot wait to
share it with all of you.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.800
While this is not how we
expected to spend our last week,

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.480
we hope that this celebration
is able to bring together

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:56.020
the Class of 2020, bridging
social distance and lost time

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.340
to the extent possible.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:01.470
We hope that your family,
friends, and loved ones

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:05.310
are able to join us to celebrate
our class' achievements,

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:07.370
memories, and friendships.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.270
We encourage you to share the link

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:11.800
to the Yale Commencement website with them

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:15.570
and to remember to use
the hashtag #Yale2020

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:19.400
to share your thoughts
and emotions as you watch.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.790
Thank you all for joining us this week.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.230
We hope that you are safe and healthy

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.370
and we are sending you all our love,

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.903
support, and congratulations.

